  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Find $\\int \u27e8\\frac{3}{t},\\frac{5}{{t}^{2}}\u27e9\\text{d}t.$",
  "worked_solution": "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \u27e8\\frac{3}{t},\\,\\frac{5}{{t}^{2}}\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & =\u27e8\\int \\frac{3}{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int \\frac{5}{{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|t|+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{5}{t}+{c}_{2}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|t|,\\,-\\frac{5}{t}\u27e9+\u27e8{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|t|,\\,-\\frac{5}{t}\u27e9+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
